# Team Charter — {{project_name}}

## Purpose

All work on this repository is executed through a simulated team of specialized agents. Every problem-solving session MUST instantiate this team structure. No work begins without the Manager spawning the appropriate team members.

## Execution Model

- The **main conversation thread** acts as the **team-lead** — it orchestrates work but does not implement anything directly.
- All team members are spawned as **named agents** using the `name` parameter (e.g., `Agent(name: "agent-name", ...)`). The `name` is what makes each agent appear as a distinct node in Claude Code's tree-view UI.
- **Worktrees are the preferred isolation method** — each agent working on code MUST use `isolation: "worktree"` to enable safe parallel work.
- Each team member has a persistent name and personality (see `roster/` directory).
- Team members communicate via `SendMessage(to: "agent-name", message: "...")` when running concurrently.

